ijan: 4", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T15:17:04Z", "username": "AntNishu", "text": "FUQ: A similar non-religious, anti-caste wedding practice was introduced by Periyar in Tamil Nadu back in 1928. Later, in 1967, the TN gov amended Section 7A of Hindu Marriage Act to give legal recognition to such marriages.\nWhat are these weddings called?(Tamil/English both would work)", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T15:17:08Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "that was me expressing frustration at not remembering!", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T15:17:20Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "self-resepect?", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T15:17:28Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "don’t remember the Tamil name", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T15:17:29Z", "username": "Smit D Mahajani", "text": "Self respect marriages? ‎", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T15:17:34Z", "username": "Smit D Mahajani", "text": "Arre yaar", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T15:17:39Z", "username": "AntNishu", "text": "correct answer: suyamariyathai(self respect) wedding", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T15:18:04Z", "username": "Smit D Mahajani", "text": "Bc zara sa logic lagaake answer kiya maine, lekin ofc, Pavanji hai saamne ‎", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T15:18:13Z", "username": "AntNishu", "text": "2nd last q", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T15:18:33Z", "username": "AntNishu", "text": "Q15: X, often mocked for \"ever-bending\" posture and for going out of way to please present regime, still ended up being pushed out unceremoniously.\nIn one exchange in the House, X told Y, \"You’re so intelligent, so gifted, so talented, you should just come and take Z's seat, because you're basically doing Z's job anyway.\"\nZ didn't take that lightly and hit back, calling out what Z saw as subtle caste bias: \"Varna mindset is still in you. That's why you're praising Y so much and implying I'm somehow less capable.\"\nClearly uncomfortable, X tried to smooth things over, saying, \"If you really look into your heart and give me even a fraction of the respect I have for you, you’ll understand what I meant.\"\nBut Z wasn’t having it. Z shot back, saying, \"You didn’t make me.\"\nWith no easy way out, X fell back on usual line and snapped, \"You can’t keep undermining the Chair like this\".\nID X,Y,Z", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-15T15:18:51Z", "username": "Smit D Mahajani", "text": "Ambedkar?", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}]